cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  QPMix is derivative work based on QMix.  If you use QPMix in published
  work, please cite the QMix papers listed under `references` below.
title: "QPMix: fast multi-tone spectral domain analysis of SIS quasiparticle mixers"
abstract: >-
  QPMix simulates the quasiparticle tunneling currents in SIS junctions
  using multi-tone spectral domain analysis.  It is a re-engineered
  derivative of QMix (Garrett & Yassin) with FFT-based phase-factor
  coefficients, uniform-grid response-function interpolation, cache-blocked
  parallel kernels and Broyden-accelerated harmonic balance.
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/xHexlabx/QPMix"
keywords:
  - SIS mixers
  - radio astronomy
  - superconducting detectors
  - terahertz instrumentation
  - harmonic balance
authors:
  - alias: HexTex
